' A real, ordinary ArcoBASIC program meant to be compiled BY the Fission
' Compiler Substrate's own native x86-64 backend (fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas)
' -- see fission/tests/native_programs/hello_native.abas's own header
' comment for the directory convention.
'
' Real Bytes.* (confirmed directly in the oracle: a "Bytes" value is just
' an ordinary Array:Number, no separate runtime representation of its own)
' and Path.Join (real `std::filesystem::path::operator/=` semantics: an
' absolute right side replaces the whole path; otherwise the two segments
' concatenate with exactly one "/" between them). Bytes.SetU8 is a real,
' disclosed exception to this backend's own "no array mutation" scope --
' it mutates one EXISTING element in place, never changing the array's own
' length, so it needs none of the growable-array representation change
' real Array.Push/etc. would.
'
' Real, disclosed scope: Bytes.New is scoped to its real 2-argument form
' (size, fill) only; Path.Home is NOT implemented at all -- it needs the
' real process ENVP block, and this backend's own `_start` entry point
' does not capture argv/envp from the stack yet (a real, separate, larger,
' disclosed undertaking).
'
' Expected output verified against legacy `ArcoFission compile-run` on this
' identical source as the equivalence-testing oracle.
b = Bytes.New(4, 7)
PRINT b
PRINT Bytes.Length(b)
PRINT Bytes.GetU8(b, 0)
b2 = Bytes.SetU8(b, 1, 300)
PRINT b2
PRINT Bytes.GetU8(b, 1)
raw = Bytes.FromText("Hi!")
PRINT raw
back = Bytes.ToText(raw)
PRINT back
PRINT Path.Join("a", "b")
PRINT Path.Join("a/", "b")
PRINT Path.Join("a", "/b")
PRINT Path.Join("", "b")
